5:/**
6: * The floor of the "no question ever blocks an application" policy.
7: *
8: * Every other source having nothing is not a reason to stop, and it is also not
9: * a licence to guess: for the two questions with a legal consequence the answer
10: * is fixed at the negative, which asserts nothing the candidate cannot back.
11: * These tests exist to make the positive impossible to introduce by accident —
12: * a regex loosened the wrong way is how "not authorized" becomes "authorized".
13: */
14:describe("conservativeDefaultAnswer: legal status", () => {
15:  const authorizationWordings = [
16:    "Are you authorized to work in the United States?",
17:    "Are you legally authorized to work in the United States without restriction?",
18:    "Do you have the right to work in the USA?",
19:    "Are you eligible to work in the US?",
20:    "United States work authorization?",
21:  ];
